"""renovation-inventory -- every tracked path of the distribution and of the
EmulationStation fork, with its area, provenance tier, language, lines, last
commits and reachability by the images the Makefile builds (M6.P1, #641).

  tools/renovation-inventory [--distribution DIR] [--es DIR]
      [--areas docs/reviews/areas.json] [--plans DIR]
      [--out docs/reviews/inventory.json] [--markdown docs/reviews/inventory.md]
      [--inject-path PATH ...] [--no-write]
  tools/renovation-inventory --self-test

Prints, and exits 1 unless each pair agrees and both counters are 0:
  paths: N (git ls-files: N)
  es-paths: N (git ls-files: N)
  patches: N (find: N)
  unassigned: N
  ambiguous: N

Exit 2 when it cannot run (a git command, a plan, a missing input).

Rules (docs/reviews/README.md, the futro of 2026-10-22):

- The inventory reads committed trees: the distribution at its HEAD, the ES
  checkout at its HEAD (a detached worktree at the pin). Each total is checked
  against `git ls-files` there, so staged-but-uncommitted paths fail the run.
- Areas: a glob is relative to the distribution unless prefixed `es:`; a glob
  prefixed `!` excludes within its own area; `**` crosses `/`, `*` and `?`
  stay inside a segment, `{a,b}` alternates literal text. A path must match
  exactly one area: none counts as `unassigned`, two or more as `ambiguous`.
  A bare `**` on the distribution is refused, since it would make
  `unassigned` 0 whatever the tree held.
- Tiers: fork-own is `git diff --name-only <merge-base> HEAD` (the merge base
  with upstream/next, or on ES with rocknix/master); a fork-own path that
  upstream also changed since the base carries `overlap`. Every other path is
  upstream-carried. Every `*.patch` and kernel `linux*.conf` under packages/
  or projects/ is vendor-carried, `tier_note: fork-written` when fork-own.
- Reachability: `tools/viewplan` per device and arch the Makefile builds,
  `image` for the 64-bit plans and `arm` (projects/ROCKNIX/packages/virtual/arm)
  for 32-bit where the device's ENABLE_32BIT is true, with PROJECT, DEVICE
  and ARCH always set, run by default in the build image the Makefile pins
  by digest (it must be local; `--runner host` is the explicit alternative,
  recorded in the header): the host lacks xmlstarlet, which
  distributions/ROCKNIX/config/functions needs for SUBDEVICES, and a host plan
  silently drops every subdevice bootloader. The checkout is mounted
  read-only and BUILD_DIR sits in the container's /tmp; on the host BUILD_DIR
  is a directory this tool owns. Either way the run fails if the checkout's
  ignored set changes. Each package in a plan is
  then sourced with config/functions' `source_package`, and its PKG_DIR,
  PKG_VERSION and PKG_PATCH_DIRS give the patch directories scripts/unpack
  would apply, by unpack's own rules. A path inside a package directory is
  reached when that directory is a plan package's PKG_DIR (a patch only when
  its directory is selected); a generic package.mk sourced by a reached
  override is reached with it; a device's own files are reached by that
  device's plans; projects/ROCKNIX's bootloader, filesystem, options and
  config.xml by every plan; ES by the plans that build emulationstation.
  `reach` is `shipped` (a shipped device's plan), `unshipped` (only other
  devices' plans), `unreached` (a package or project path no plan reaches),
  or `n/a` (a path no image plan can hold: the engine, tools, doctrine,
  records). Reachability errs toward reached: a file in a reached package is
  reached even if its recipe installs it only for some devices.
"""

